Current buggy code: uses forward `end` without adjusting, and need(end>offset||...) breaks offset===text.length? Actually offset===text.length allowed. But end==offset with offset<length: rejects (empty non-EOF slice rejected — but with backward move, could still progress? If max_chars>=1 and offset<length, end>offset always unless surrogate at offset... offset start is validated not interior, so char at offset is fine; end=offset+1 always ≥. Hmm splitPair(end) means end is between pair; move end back to end-1. Then end-1>offset unless offset=end-1 i.e., offset+1 = end, meaning max_chars=1 and text[offset] is high surrogate with low at offset+1... wait splitPair(position) checks text[position-1] high, text[position] low. end=offset+1 splits if text[offset] high and text[offset+1] low. Moving back gives end=offset, no progress → reject. Good.

